verdict
The bug is the predicate at source/priority-queue.ts line 93: const index = this.#findIndex(element => element.id !== id); should be element.id === id to find the target element. Dequeue and compaction are not the cause; dequeues only null consumed slots and advance #head, so live indices remain stable, and #findIndex starts at #head. The public PQueue.setPriority wrapper already searches #waitingTasks by strict id equality before delegating, so the broken matching is in the default queue class.

